WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.652
A physical dosage form releases medicine over time.

00:00:04.652 --> 00:00:08.754
A mathematical model tries to describe that changing process.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:19.373
Formulation composition, geometry and transport assumptions affect simulated

00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:24.404
release. The selected equations embody choices that need scrutiny.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.490
The book chapter examines simulation of drug release

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.931
and performance prediction using virtual models within pharmaceutical development.

00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:49.589
Without calibration and suitable validation, a model can

00:00:49.589 --> 00:00:53.253
produce elegant curves and still make poor predictions.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.946
Mechanistic assumptions, parameter uncertainty and extrapolation beyond

00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:07.592
known experiments all limit credible digital performance forecasts.

00:01:13.758 --> 00:01:16.915
A defensible virtual model can guide test

00:01:16.915 --> 00:01:20.073
design, but the laboratory decides what survives.
